A checkbox's and a toggle's `@change` carries a `ToggleEvent`, and its
`checked` is the control's state after the flip, on every target.

Both used to be declared with a `ChangeEvent`, whose `value` is a string no
host has for an on/off control. So `e.value` was whatever each target happened
to spell: `"on"` on html, a `bool` assigned to a string on fyne and gtk4
(`box_change_handler(b bool) { got = b }`), an undefined `e` on bubbletea and
on gtk4's toggle, `on.value` on android. The payload is now each host's own
answer: `e.target.checked`, fyne's `OnChanged(b bool)`, gtk4's
`gtk_check_button_get_active` and `gtk_switch_get_active`, Compose's
`onCheckedChange` argument, and on bubbletea the override's own `!checked`.

The bound `:checked` reads the same payload rather than toggling. A toggle
assumed the event fires once per user flip, and fyne's `SetChecked` inside the
box's own `OnChanged` fired it again, flipping the bound var back and forth
until the stack ran out. bubbletea is the target with no host state to report,
so its override computes the new state once and both the write-back and the
payload read that one value: computed twice, the write-back flipped the var and
the payload flipped it back.

gtk4's switch reports a flip only through GObject's `notify::active`, whose
callback is `(instance, pspec, user_data)`, so `sngl_connect` takes a second
trampoline for a notification. Before it the toggle was wired to nothing.

A test drives each through the platform's input path, handing the payload
where the host would have it: onto the element on html, into the widget's
state on gtk4 (setting it is what fires the signal), into the callback on fyne.
bubbletea and android press the key and click the control, which flips it
whatever the payload says, so the test flips from the state it is in.

deny * `\bChangeEvent\b` -- neither control's payload is a ChangeEvent any more
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `bool\(C\.` -- a gboolean is C.int, which Go converts to no bool
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `\be\.` -- the payload is taken apart where it is built; no event reaches the key case
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:test"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main node {
    var on = false
    var lit = false
    var seen = "none"
    vbox {
        checkbox #box(:checked=on, label="a", @change(e) { seen = "box {e.checked} {on}" })
        toggle #sw(checked=lit, label="b", @change(e) {
            lit = e.checked
            seen = "sw {e.checked}"
        })
        text(value=seen)
    }
}

func testCheckboxCarriesChecked(t Test, c main) {
    c.box.change({checked=true})
    t.assert(c.seen == "box true true")
    t.assert(c.on == true)
    c.box.change({checked=false})
    t.assert(c.seen == "box false false")
    t.assert(c.on == false)
}

func testToggleCarriesChecked(t Test, c main) {
    c.sw.change({checked=true})
    t.assert(c.seen == "sw true")
    t.assert(c.lit == true)
    c.sw.change({checked=false})
    t.assert(c.seen == "sw false")
    t.assert(c.lit == false)
}

window {
    main
}
